<section class="section">

    <div class="timeline">

        <div class="timeline-item">

            <div class="timeline-number">01</div>

            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">CONCEPT</p>
                <h2>Understanding the challenge</h2>

                <p>
                    We began by studying the purpose of lunar packaging
                    and identifying ways that the structure could continue
                    to be useful after delivery.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>


        <div class="timeline-item">

            <div class="timeline-number">02</div>

            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">DESIGN</p>
                <h2>Developing the locker</h2>

                <p>
                    We created a CAD model and developed a modular structure
                    that could be assembled, disassembled, and reused.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>


        <div class="timeline-item">

            <div class="timeline-number">03</div>

            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">PROTOTYPE</p>
                <h2>Building at 1/3 scale</h2>

                <p>
                    A physical prototype will allow us to evaluate the
                    structure and identify areas that need improvement.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>


        <div class="timeline-item">

            <div class="timeline-number">04</div>

            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">TESTING</p>
                <h2>Testing the structure</h2>

                <p>
                    Our planned testing includes a 1 kg water-bag drop
                    from 50 cm onto both a flat side and a corner.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

</section>


<section class="dark-section">

    <div class="section-heading center">

        <p class="eyebrow">TESTING</p>

        <h2>1 kg / 50 cm</h2>

        <p>
            Testing will help us determine how the prototype responds
            to impact and where improvements may be necessary.
        </p>

    </div>


    <div class="test-grid">

        <div class="test-card">
            <strong>01</strong>
            <h3>FLAT SIDE</h3>
            <p>Drop the test load onto a flat side of the prototype.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="test-card">
            <strong>02</strong>
            <h3>CORNER</h3>
            <p>Drop the test load onto a corner of the prototype.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="test-card">
            <strong>03</strong>
            <h3>OBSERVE</h3>
            <p>Record structural changes and areas of failure.</p>
        </div>

    </div>

</section>


